---
description: Every behavior change ships with a colocated *.check.ts and a passing check script.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Test coverage every time

Do not ship a behavior change without automated coverage in the same change. If you add or change logic, add or update a check. Do not finish with “tests later”.

This repo uses colocated Node self-checks, not Vitest/Jest. Keep that.

```
# ❌ BAD — new helper, no check
src/lib/period-bounds.ts

# ✅ GOOD — helper plus colocated check, wired in package.json
src/lib/period-bounds.ts
src/lib/period-bounds.check.ts
```

- Colocate `foo.check.ts` next to `foo.ts` (same folder). Name it after the module, e.g. `pagination.check.ts`.
- Assert with a small local helper that **throws** on mismatch. End with `console.log("….check.ts: ok")`.
- Run with `node --experimental-strip-types path/to/file.check.ts`. Wire a `check:` script (or append to existing `check` / `lint`) in that package’s `package.json`.
- Changing covered behavior means **updating the check**, not deleting assertions.
- Extract testable logic (pure functions, SQL filters, routers, schemas, parsers) out of UI. Do not add React Testing Library or a new test runner.
- API DB checks use `createTestDb` / `withUser` like `projects.filters.check.ts`.
- Run the relevant `pnpm --filter <pkg> check…` and keep it green before declaring done.

**Out of scope** (no new check file): copy-only i18n catalog edits, comments, Cursor rules, docs, and CSS with no behavior change. Still run existing checks if those files are already covered (e.g. `check:i18n`).
